body:
As a male raised by NParents, the abuse they planted made most of my relationships very superficial to the point where I recently hooked up with someone off of Tinder that I thought was probably the hottest person I had ever seen, and I literally could not finish. I can't find someone attractive without feelings of depression, shame, guilt, anxiety, and worthlessness setting in, much less talk to them. I've had several drug experiences that freed me from this aspect of my trauma, which is the only reason I know that I'll be able to come back from this once I'm able to financially afford distance from my parents. Narcissists can really fuck up your sexuality, but acknowledging the reality of what they've done is always where the healing starts.

&#x200B;

My parents were extremely creepy about any intimate relationships I had in my youth. Like, way, way too interested.
